#only("1-")[Let's understand this better:]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Overconfidence bias occurs when investors overestimate their knowledge or ability to predict market movements 🧠]
#only("3-")[- They believe they can consistently outperform the market 📈]
#only("4-")[- This leads to excessive trading, as they think they can time the market 🕰️]
#only("5-")[- Excessive trading often results in lower returns due to increased transaction costs and poor timing decisions 💸]

#only("1")[#voiceover("Let's dive a bit deeper into overconfidence bias and its consequences.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("Overconfidence bias occurs when investors overestimate their knowledge or ability to predict market movements. They believe they have superior skills or information compared to others.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("This leads them to think they can consistently outperform the market, beating average returns.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("As a result, overconfident investors often engage in excessive trading. They believe they can time the market, knowing when to buy and sell for maximum profit.")]
#only("5")[#voiceover("However, excessive trading frequently leads to lower returns. This is due to increased transaction costs from frequent trades and poor timing decisions based on overconfidence rather than market realities.")]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Avoiding Overconfidence Bias]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[How can investors avoid overconfidence bias? 🤔]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Acknowledge the limits of your knowledge and predictive ability 🧠]
#only("3-")[- Rely on data and objective analysis rather than gut feelings 📊]
#only("4-")[- Diversify your portfolio to spread risk 🗂️]
#only("5-")[- Stick to a long-term investment strategy rather than trying to time the market 📆]

#only("1")[#voiceover("So how can investors avoid falling prey to overconfidence bias?")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("First, it's important to acknowledge the limits of your own knowledge and ability to predict the market. No one can consistently predict market movements with perfect accuracy.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("Instead of relying on gut feelings or hunches, base your investment decisions on data and objective analysis. Look at company financials, market trends, and economic indicators.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("Diversifying your portfolio across different asset classes and sectors can also help mitigate the impact of overconfidence. If one investment performs poorly, others may compensate.")]
#only("5")[#voiceover("Finally, stick to a long-term investment strategy rather than trying to time the market. Timing the market is notoriously difficult, even for professional investors. A steady, long-term approach is often more effective.")]
]

